 "notes": "Paper derives new 90% CL exclusion limits on dark photon kinetic mixing from Hinode XRT solar X-ray telescope data, using (1) calibration 'darks' as a space-based helioscope and (2) a 2012 solar eclipse image as a light-shining-through-the-Moon setup. Full exclusion curves are in figures 5 and 8 (not tabulated). Extracted numerical anchors from text: benchmark points stated to lie close to the exclusion limit of the radial+spectral analysis without background subtraction: (400 eV, 6.1e-11), (15 eV, 1.2e-10), (1 eV, 1.5e-8). From Table 1: darks best sensitivity eps=1e-9 at m=1 eV (data-driven background subtraction improves limits by >1 order of magnitude over naive counting); eclipse sensitivity eps=4e-8 at m=1 eV with kink (low-mass sensitivity loss) at m~2e-6 eV; darks kink at m~3e-2 eV. The eclipse point at 2e-6 eV approximates the flat region of the eclipse limit extending down to the kink. No DM density assumption (solar-produced DPs, not halo DM). Points mix different analyses; full curves require plot digitization, hence moderate confidence. | vector-trace candidate: figure_5.pdf colour (0.5, 0.0, 0.6), 544 pts (selected among 3) | selector: vector_trace over text (quality (1, 1, 1, 1, 3.5, 0, 0.85, 544))",
